Appendix E. Derivation of the Robust Inventory Buffer Size via Dualization

For completeness, we show a direct dual derivation of the worst‑case cumulative demand bound used in Lemma 4.2. The maximum of $\sum_{t=1}^L \bar d + \delta z_t$ subject to $\sum |z_t| \le \Gamma$, $|z_t| \le 1$ can be found by linear programming:

\max_{z_t} \sum_{t=1}^L \delta z_t \quad \text{s.t.} \quad \sum_{t} u_t \le \Gamma,\; -u_t \le z_t \le u_t,\; u_t \le 1.

By introducing $u_t = |z_t|$, the LP becomes maximizing $\delta \sum_t z_t$ with $z_t \le u_t$, $-z_t \le u_t$, $\sum u_t \le \Gamma$, $u_t \le 1$. The dual will show the maximum is $\delta \cdot \min(\Gamma, L)$, and the extremal $z_t$ set $z_t = 1$ for $\min(\Gamma,L)$ periods and $0$ otherwise. The result is used in Appendix B.4.

